      "claim": "L4 Caco-2 records for polar ribonucleoside/cytidine analogs show low permeability: levovirin 0.12×10^-6 cm/s (C50) and gemcitabine <1×10^-6 / 0.99×10^-6 cm/s (C52, C58), supporting poor passive absorption for the highly polar query.",
      "card_ids": ["C50","C52","C58"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L5 bidirectional transport records show low A→B permeability and efflux for nucleoside analogs: EFdA A→B ~4-6×10^-7 cm/s (C60, C64), GS-441524 A→B 0.229×10^-6 cm/s with BCRP/MDR1 efflux (C62, C65, C67, C70), and cladribine BCRP-mediated efflux (C59, C68, C69), indicating gut-wall efflux as a plausible presystemic loss mechanism.",
      "card_ids": ["C60","C62","C64","C65","C67","C70","C59","C68","C69"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L1 gold outcomes for other nucleoside scaffolds are mixed: emtricitabine 92% (C16, C33) and didanosine 38% (C13, C32) show some nucleosides reach F≥20%, but acyclovir is at 20% (C06); these scaffolds differ from the ribonucleoside query and do not affirmatively establish F≥20% for 5-azacytidine.",
      "card_ids": ["C16","C33","C13","C32","C06"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 hepatic clearance records for other nucleosides (GS-441524 not a CYP substrate, C78/C80; zidovudine low UGT intrinsic clearance, C71-C77/C79/C82) do not measure the query's cytidine deaminase pathway and are of low transferability; they do not provide affirmative evidence for F<20% or F≥20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C78","C80","C71","C72","C73","C74","C75","C76","C77","C79","C82"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "hepatic_clearance_metabolic_stability",
      "applicability": "low",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C71","C72","C73","C74","C75","C76","C77","C78","C79","C80","C81","C82"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement for 5-azacytidine is present in the supplied records.",
    "No query-specific Caco-2/MDCK permeability, efflux, or intestinal metabolism data; all L4/L5 records are for analog nucleosides with inferred transferability.",
    "Cytidine deaminase-mediated first-pass metabolism and gut-wall metabolism for the query are not directly measured; L6 records cover CYP and UGT pathways only.",
    "Possible CNT/ENT transporter-mediated uptake for the query is not directly measured; L5 substrate records for gemcitabine/NHC are analog evidence only.",
    "The query_prior reasoning text names guanosine, but the canonical SMILES corresponds to 5-azacytidine; the prior is treated only as an uncertain physicochemical prior.",
    "High-F records for emtricitabine/didanosine come from different nucleoside scaffolds; their transferability to the ribonucleoside query is limited."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Prediction remains low with moderate confidence. L4/L5 analog permeability and efflux records (levovirin, gemcitabine, EFdA, GS-441524, cladribine) provide coherent measured absorption/efflux evidence for poor oral absorption of polar nucleosides, and the physicochemical prior is unfavorable. L6 hepatic clearance records for other nucleosides are low-transferability and do not address the query's cytidine deaminase pathway, so they do not change the decision."
}

